# Do not download the Cypress browser binary on install.
#
# It is ~300 MB, and almost nothing that installs this project needs it: not a
# Vercel build, not the unit CI job, not a contributor who only runs `npm test`.
# Only the end-to-end job needs it, and it fetches it in a step of its own.
#
# This lives here rather than in vercel.json's installCommand, which is where it
# started: npm reads .npmrc no matter who invokes it or how, so a build platform
# that runs its own install command -- a Vercel dashboard setting overrides
# vercel.json, for instance -- still gets this. A setting that only applies when
# the command is spelled the way you expect is not a setting you can rely on.
#
# Cypress reads npm config as well as the environment, so `cypress_install_binary`
# here has the same effect as CYPRESS_INSTALL_BINARY=0 in the environment. The
# corollary is that npm-invoked installs cannot opt back in by setting the
# environment variable -- npm's project config wins over an env var it considers
# unset -- which is why the e2e job calls the Cypress binary directly.
cypress_install_binary=0
